{"Malformed Zod schema in parseRefreshTokenResponse uses computed keys based on z.string().toString() which creates literal string keys like 'z.string()' instead of matching expected token fields like expiry_date or expires_in, causing validation failures": 0.8513390421867371, "parseRefreshTokenResponse returns Zod SafeParseReturn object but code stores it directly to DB via prisma.credential.update, corrupting credential structure by storing wrapper object instead of parsed data": 0.6960242986679077, "refreshOAuthTokens returns inconsistent types - sometimes returns refreshFunction's return value (axios response, library object, or string) and sometimes returns node-fetch Response, breaking callers that expect specific shapes": 0.9005908966064453, "Webhook handler doesn't validate webhook encryption key before decrypting - if CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY is missing or malformed, symmetricDecrypt is called with empty string fallback, causing 500s and possible lost webhook deliveries": 0.8038276433944702, "Salesforce CalendarService getClient constructs jsforce.Connection using stale credentialKey values instead of newly refreshed accessTokenParsed.data after token refresh, causing authentication errors": 0.8157967329025269, ".env.example recommends 'openssl rand -base64 24' for AES-256 key but this produces incorrect length (should be 32 bytes), and webhook handler has no runtime length/format validation for encryption key": 0.5950121283531189}